  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Both roles of the Shared Signals Framework. As a transmitter: publish configuration discovery, let receivers create, read, update and delete event streams, add and remove the subjects each stream is about, answer verification requests, and deliver events by push or hold them for poll. As a receiver: find a transmitter, open and configure a stream, manage its subjects, request verification and consume events from either delivery mode. Built over the Security Events core, with the CAEP and RISC dictionaries naming the events, so two parties agree on what an event means without a private contract. An event outbox on Redis is available for transmitters that run as several replicas. Full details: https://github.com/Abblix/Oidc.Server/releases/tag/v2.4",
